meta {
  name: OmzettenNaarOrder
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/offerte/2161043/1/omzetten-naar-order
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Iteratie D - Offerte->Order conversie. Converts offerte 2161043/1 (a
  LunaNew test offerte with at least one overdraagbare item line) into a
  new bon. Response shape:
  {bonnr, offnr, versie, offerteStempel, aantalLijnenOvergenomen,
  aantalLedLijnenOvergenomen, totBtw, totaalBasis, totaalInclBtw}.

  NOTE: this request is NOT idempotent - offnr 2161043/1 can only be
  converted once (a second run will 409, see
  OmzettenNaarOrderAlreadyConverted409.bru). If you need to re-run this
  request, pick a different open (stempel "O") offerte/versie with at
  least one transferable line, update the URL, and update
  OmzettenNaarOrderAlreadyConverted409.bru to match.

  Body is not read by the server - {} is sent to keep the request
  self-documenting; any JSON object (even {}) satisfies the handler's
  "must be a JSON object" body check.
}
